        "answer": {
          "short": "$17.6\\text{ m}$. Find the ground distances using the shared height, then apply the cosine rule in $\\triangle AOB$.",
          "worked": "In the vertical right triangles:\n$$\\begin{align*}AO&=10\\cos53^\\circ\\\\\\tan30^\\circ&=\\frac{OH}{OB}\\\\OB&=\\frac{10\\sin53^\\circ}{\\tan30^\\circ}.\\end{align*}$$\nUse the cosine rule in $\\triangle AOB$, retaining unrounded lengths:\n$$\\begin{align*}AB^2&=AO^2+OB^2-2(AO)(OB)\\cos120^\\circ\\\\AB^2&\\approx310.811441\\\\AB&\\approx17.6\\text{ m}.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 78
